# Audit Logging Policy

Use `logAudit()` from `$lib/server/services/auditLog` for actions that modify data in sensitive or admin contexts.

## Actions That MUST Be Audit Logged

- All admin panel mutations (team status changes, player bans, manual payment marks, match overrides)
- Payment-related actions (manual payment marks, refunds)
- Permission/role changes
- Season/division configuration changes
- Any action performed on behalf of another user

## Actions That Do NOT Need Audit Logging

- Normal user actions on their own resources (editing own team, leaving team)
- Read-only operations
- Signup/registration flows (these have their own paper trail via DB records)

## Usage

```typescript
import { logAudit, AuditCategory, AuditAction } from '$lib/server/services/auditLog';

await logAudit({
  actorId: locals.user.steamId,
  actorRole: locals.user.permissionLevel,
  category: AuditCategory.TEAM,
  action: AuditAction.TEAM_STATUS_CHANGED,
  targetType: 'Team',
  targetId: String(teamId),
  metadata: { oldStatus, newStatus },
  ipAddress: getClientAddress(),
});
```
